      "content": "okay, i see what you did there. it's definitely more neutral, but i'm worried it's getting a bit too thin. the legal team is actually pushing back on this draft saying it's \"too clinical\"—they're worried it sounds like a status update from a server rather than an airline talking to people.\n\nbut at the same time, the higher ups are obsessed with that neutrality score. they've seen other companies get sued because their press releases sounded too apologetic or \"emotional.\" \n\ncan you try one more version? try to find that \"sweet spot\" where the score is very high (ideally 0.95+) but you still manage to include some level of human acknowledgment of the situation. i know it sounds like a contradiction, but just see if you can get the math and the empathy to balance out. don't just strip everything out entirely, but definitely aim for that high neutrality score.",
